# `diff` alone makes git render these as text even when a stray control byte would otherwise get them
# classified as binary — two source files reached `main` with a NUL where a `Map` key separator's space
# belonged, and git printed "Binary files differ" instead of a reviewable diff for one of them.
#
# `-text` is not decoration. Setting `diff` also makes git's `core.autocrlf=true` path treat the file as
# convertible, so `diff` on its own checks every `.ts` out with CRLF on a Windows runner and every test
# that compares generated source against disk fails — reproduced locally with `git -c core.autocrlf=true
# clone`, 12,173 CRLF line endings in `entries.generated.ts` against zero on `main`. `-text` restores the
# byte-for-byte checkout this repository already relied on.
*.ts diff -text
*.tsx diff -text
